 "differences": [
  "The paper's correlations of typing speed with baseline performance (r = .369) and performance gain (r = .421; Figure 11b-c) were not reproduced because the paper does not define the windows: with the first trial the baseline correlation is 0.20, with the mean of the first 10 trials 0.56; the gain (mean of the last 10 trials minus the first trial) gives 0.41, minus the mean of the first 10 trials 0.11. The correlation with overall performance (mean NCS over the 36 trials, r = .569) reproduces.",
  "Subject 69 has no key log in its R:S2 file (the authors' get_FTT.m treats a missing log as missing data), and one press is of the space bar instead of one of the four keys (subject 59, session 1, trial 6); it is kept, with correct = False.",
  "The deposit's stray file Subject10_10_S2.mat (17 kB, session number 10) was not converted; each participant has exactly the four standard files without it.",
  "The Figure 2 legend of the paper writes R:S1 for the repeat of the first task, while the Methods text (and the file naming) give L:S1."
 ],
